Name     edge2latch16v8;
Partno   x;
Date     2026-11-21;
Revision 1;
Designer galtools;
Company  x;
Assembly x;
Location x;
Device   g16v8ma;

/* Test design: GAL16V8, an edge detector made from the delay of two
   outputs, which a real chip takes.  TD is a copy of T on a pin of its
   own, one output delay late, and TD2 a copy of TD, two late.  The term
   !T & TD2 is true for those two delays after T falls, and Q takes !D
   then: a flip-flop clocked by the falling edge of T, without a clock
   pin.  Q is back at the array after one delay, while the term is still
   true, and EN & Q & !D holds it from then on.  While EN is low Q is
   clear.  In edgelatch16v8 the term is true for one delay only, and a
   real GAL16V8 never took the edge.

   Compile with cupl -jaxm0: the last term of Q only holds it while
   another takes over, and minimising removes it. */

Pin 2  = EN;
Pin 3  = D;
Pin 4  = T;
Pin 5  = A;
Pin 6  = X;
Pin 14 = TD2;
Pin 15 = Z;
Pin 16 = TD;
Pin 17 = Q;
Pin 18 = Y;

TD = T;
TD2 = TD;
Q = EN & !D & !T & TD2
  # EN & Q & !TD2
  # EN & Q & T
  # EN & Q & !D;
Y = Q & D;
Z = A;
Z.oe = !X;
